{{also|Strecken|strécken}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|strecken}}, from {{inh|de|goh|strecken}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*strakkjan}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|[ˈʃtʁɛkŋ̩]|[ˈʃtʁɛkən]}}
* {{audio|de|De-strecken.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[stretch]] (oneself, for example before exercise or after waking up)
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[stretch]] (a specific body part)
#: {{ux|de|Sie '''streckte''' ihre müden Glieder.|She '''stretched''' her tired limbs.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[extend]] (a body part)
#: {{ux|de|Sie '''streckte''' den Hals, um über den Zaun zu sehen.|She '''craned''' her neck to see over the fence.}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive|or|transitive}} to [[stretch out]], to [[lie down]]
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''streckte''' mich auf dem Sofa aus und schlief ein.|I '''stretched out''' on the sofa and fell asleep.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[elongate]], [[lengthen]]
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[dilute]], [[cut]]
#: {{ux|de|Er '''streckte''' den Wein mit Wasser.|He '''diluted''' the wine with water.}}

